WEBVTT

00:21:28.996 --> 00:21:32.288
and in captive chimps as well,
for the most part.

00:21:33.079 --> 00:21:35.579
And then what about what
about body language?

00:21:35.579 --> 00:21:39.038
What do we learn about the way that
the chimps communicate through

00:21:39.288 --> 00:21:43.079
the gestures they make? I'm curious about
other human analogs and parallels there.

00:21:44.329 --> 00:21:47.829
I mean, if you watch chimpanzees
communicating nonverbally,

00:21:48.288 --> 00:21:51.871
you more or less know exactly what they're
doing because we do the same.

00:21:52.121 --> 00:21:55.579
I mean, we we really do. We shake fists.

00:21:55.579 --> 00:22:00.579
We if you don't like something, you make
that flapping, flapping movement.